<p>Wardrobes and linen cupboards hide dust, dropped buttons and musty smells until you pull everything out. A seasonal reset — not necessarily a whole-house spring clean — keeps clothes fresher and makes <a href="{{guide:bedroom-dust-mite-reduction}}">allergy-friendly bedrooms</a> easier to maintain.</p>
<div class="cc-takeaways"><p class="cc-takeaways__title">Key takeaways</p><ul><li>Empty one section at a time so you don’t lose momentum.</li><li>Vacuum floors, shelves and wardrobe tracks before replacing items.</li><li>Wash or air bedding before it goes back on shelves.</li><li>Pair with a <a href="{{service:deep-cleaning}}">deep clean</a> if bedrooms haven’t been done properly in years.</li></ul></div>
