<p>Sort into keep, donate and recycle. If you haven’t worn it in a year and it isn’t occasion wear, let it go. Bag donations straight to the car boot so they don’t creep back.</p>
<h2>Clean the empty space</h2>
<p>Dust shelf tops, wipe rails, and vacuum carpet or laminate inside fitted wardrobes. Wipe down plastic storage boxes — they attract static dust.</p>
<h2>Linen cupboard</h2>
<p>Wash duvet covers and towels even if they look clean; folds trap stale air. Note what you’re short of before “buy more” trips. Label shelves if several people share a bathroom.</p>
<h2>Storage tips</h2>
<p>Breathable garment bags beat dry-cleaner plastic. Cedar blocks or lavender sachets help moths; vacuum packs save space for seasonal coats.</p>
<h2>When to book help</h2>
<p>If cupboards are part of a whole-house backlog, <a href="{{guide:when-to-book-a-deep-clean}}">book a deep clean</a> and flag bedrooms on the list. We work across <a href="{{area:hull}}">Hull</a> and East Yorkshire — <a href="{{page:contact}}">get in touch</a>.</p>
