		'content'     => <<<'HTML'
<p>Dust mites thrive in warm, humid bedrooms with plenty of skin cells in bedding and carpets. You can’t sterilise a home, but you can lower allergen levels with washing, hoovering and humidity control — especially helpful before pollen season in East Yorkshire.</p>
<div class="cc-takeaways"><p class="cc-takeaways__title">Key takeaways</p><ul><li>Wash bedding weekly at 60°C if fabrics allow, or use allergen wash additives.</li><li>Hoover mattresses and under beds monthly; use a HEPA filter if possible.</li><li>Keep humidity around 40–50% with ventilation or a dehumidifier.</li><li>Professional <a href="{{service:carpet-upholstery-cleaning}}">carpet cleaning</a> removes deep-set dust regular hoovering misses.</li></ul></div>
<h2>Bedding and pillows</h2>
<p>Wash duvets and pillows per care labels; replace pillows every few years. Encasements on mattresses help sensitive sleepers.</p>
<h2>Floors and textiles</h2>
<p>Hard floors show dust but are easier to mop; carpets need slow hoovering and periodic extraction — see <a href="{{guide:carpet-cleaning-methods-explained}}">carpet cleaning methods</a>. Curtains and upholstered headboards collect fibres; vacuum or launder seasonally.</p>
<h2>Declutter surfaces</h2>
<p>Fewer ornaments means fewer places for dust to land. A <a href="{{guide:wardrobe-and-linen-cupboard-clean}}">wardrobe clear-out</a> reduces textile dust in the room.</p>
<h2>Professional help</h2>
<p>We clean carpets and upholstery across <a href="{{area:hull}}">Hull</a> and nearby towns. <a href="{{page:contact}}">Request a quote</a> if bedrooms haven’t had a deep textile clean in years.</p>
